{"tool_name":"coregnet","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"coregnet","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/CoRegNet.html","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"This package provides methods to identify active transcriptional programs, including methods and classes to import or infer large scale co-regulatory network from transcriptomic data. The specificity of the encoded networks is to model TF cooperation. External regulation evidences (TFBS, ChIP,...) can be integrated to assess the inferred network and refine it if necessary.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:03:12Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-11T00:51:06Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.10.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:coregnet","credit":[{"email":"remy.c.nicolle@gmail.com","name":"Remy Nicolle","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8084-1173","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/CoRegNet.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Transcriptional regulatory element prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0438"}]}],"name":"CoRegNet","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btv305","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 The Author.CoRegNet is an R/Bioconductor package to analyze large-scale transcriptomic data by highlighting sets of co-regulators. Based on a transcriptomic dataset, CoRegNet can be used to: reconstruct a large-scale co-regulatory network, integrate regulation evidences such as transcription factor binding sites and ChIP data, estimate sample-specific regulator activity, identify cooperative transcription factors and analyze the sample-specific combinations of active regulators through an interactive visualization tool. In this study CoRegNet was used to identify driver regulators of bladder cancer.","authors":[{"name":"Elati M."},{"name":"Nicolle R."},{"name":"Radvanyi F."}],"citationCount":26,"date":"2015-07-31T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"CoRegNet: Reconstruction and integrated analysis of co-regulatory networks"},"pmcid":"PMC4565029","pmid":"25979476","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CoRegNet","home":"https://bio.tools/coregnet","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"1.10.0","summary":"This package provides methods to identify active transcriptional programs, including methods and classes to import or infer large scale co-regulatory network from transcriptomic data. The specificity of the encoded networks is to model TF cooperation. External regulation evidences (TFBS, ChIP,...) can be integrated to assess the inferred network and refine it if necessary.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:coregnet:1.10.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":35,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2017"},{"count":4,"year":"2018"},{"count":4,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":5,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btv305","pmcid":"PMC4565029","pmid":"25979476","ref_count":12,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":2,"year":